version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ptorrijos99/fedcausal"
url: "https://ptorrijos99.github.io/fedcausal/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  fedcausal learns causal structure from data split across sites that cannot
  share them. In FedGES each site runs greedy equivalence search on its own
  data, a coordinator fuses the resulting graphs, and only graphs and scores
  leave the sites; it takes discrete and continuous data. FedRCD recovers a
  causal order and linear coefficients under a linear non-Gaussian model from
  moment sums that each site computes on its own rows. Both run in one process
  for experiments or over Flower across machines.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - federated learning
  - greedy equivalence search
  - LiNGAM
  - cumulants

